====================================================================================
4. HOW MUCH OF EACH EFFECT ARRIVES EARLY
====================================================================================
  The loop is not re-run, so the longer the window the more the estimate assumes the
  algorithm sat still while glucose climbed. Hypoglycaemia lands early and
  hyperglycaemia accrues late, so the two sides are not equally trustworthy.

    window   covers   dTBR<70   dTBR<54     dTAR  TAR per TBR
      60m      12%     -3.35     -1.03    +8.24          2.5
     120m      23%     -5.79     -0.88   +10.75          1.9
     180m      31%     -6.33     -0.91   +17.76          2.8
     300m      42%     -6.37     -0.74   +34.07          5.3

  A rising ratio with window length is the unmodelled loop response showing up as
  hyperglycaemia the algorithm would in fact have corrected.

